codex
The concrete root cause is now clear: on the redirect cycle, a wrong-path M instruction can assert `md_start`, making `stall=1`; `i_mem_en` is then deasserted because it only allows `!stall || at_cross_boundary`. So the redirect target address is driven, but the synchronous I-memory never loads that target word. The next decoded instruction uses stale `i_mem_rdata`, corrupting the compressed decode and commit association.
codex
I’m applying a clean RTL fix in two parts: redirect must keep I-fetch enabled and must not let wrong-path M operations start or complete into `md_result_q`; separately, M-unit `done` will be delayed until its result register is already stable, so DIV/REM and MUL writeback cannot depend on simulator scheduling. This directly targets both the first full-M failure and the reported REM-result class.
apply patch
