This is an M-result bug, not a branch unit bug. The branch at `0x191e` uses `s10`; DUT’s earlier `mul s10,s6,ra` at `pc=0x18f0` wrote `0x2ec5092c`, while Spike wrote `0xbeac392c`. The later branch decision only exposes that bad MUL result. I’m drilling into the MUL operand/result path around that instruction.
