codex
The branch mismatch is a harness artifact, but deeper than one value: the DUT executes with PC offset `0`, while Spike executes the ELF at `0x1000`. The comparator can normalize AUIPC writebacks, but it cannot make Spike re-run control flow with normalized branch operands. Here the raw base delta changes `blt s10,tp`, so Spike takes a branch the DUT correctly does not. The correct harness fix is to run both machines with the same architectural PC base, not post-normalize control flow.
