 def test_phase_03_09_result_is_honest_and_sufficient():

codex
Spike cannot map RAM at zero because its built-in low memory devices overlap `[0,0x1000)`. The robust same-base fix is to run both at `0x1000`: I’m parameterizing the core/IFU reset PC with a default preserving existing RTL behavior, then the riscv-dv testbench instantiates this phase at `0x1000` and offsets I/D memory accesses back into the loaded binary image.
apply patch
